{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1784","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Infinite Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice and Bob are playing an infinite game consisting of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"sets"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each set consists of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"rounds"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". In each round, one of the players wins. The first player to win two rounds in a set wins this set. Thus, a set always ends with the score of $$$2:0$$$ or $$$2:1$$$ in favor of one of the players."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"game scenario"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" a finite string $$$s$$$ consisting of characters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'. Consider an infinite string formed with repetitions of string $$$s$$$: $$$sss \\ldots$$$ Suppose that Alice and Bob play rounds according to this infinite string, left to right. If a character of the string $$$sss \\ldots$$$ is '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', then Alice wins the round; if it's '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', Bob wins the round. As soon as one of the players wins two rounds, the set ends in their favor, and a new set starts from the next round."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define $$$a_i$$$ as the number of sets won by Alice among the first $$$i$$$ sets while playing according to the given scenario. Let's also define $$$r$$$ as the limit of ratio $$$\\frac{a_i}{i}$$$ as $$$i \\rightarrow \\infty$$$. If $$$r \\gt \\frac{1}{2}$$$, we'll say that scenario $$$s$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"winning for Alice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". If $$$r = \\frac{1}{2}$$$, we'll say that scenario $$$s$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tied"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". If $$$r \\lt \\frac{1}{2}$$$, we'll say that scenario $$$s$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"winning for Bob"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a string $$$s$$$ consisting of characters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'. Consider all possible ways of replacing every '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' with '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' or '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' to obtain a string consisting only of characters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'. Count how many of them result in a scenario winning for Alice, how many result in a tied scenario, and how many result in a scenario winning for Bob. Print these three numbers modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains a single string $$$s$$$ ($$$1 \\le |s| \\le 200$$$), consisting of characters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print three integers: how many ways result in a scenario winning for Alice, how many result in a tied scenario, and how many result in a scenario winning for Bob, modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n??\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n2\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n?aa?b\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{